<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borso d'Este</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1413–<a href="/years/1471">1471</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borso d'Este was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> from 1450. Emperor Frederick III made him Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> and Reggio in 1452, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-ii">Pope Paul II</a> made him Duke of Ferrara in 1471, shortly before his death. A lavish patron, he commissioned the illuminated Bible of Borso d'Este and the frescoes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-schifanoia">Palazzo Schifanoia</a>.</p></div>
